WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.512
A variable does not have to keep the same value forever.

00:00:03.512 --> 00:00:07.922
Python lets us assign a new value to an existing variable.

00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:10.957
At first, sales is one thousand.

00:00:10.957 --> 00:00:15.227
After the second assignment, sales becomes fifteen hundred.

00:00:15.227 --> 00:00:20.587
When Python reaches the second print statement, it uses the most recent value.

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:23.051
This is called reassignment.

00:00:23.051 --> 00:00:31.321
It is common when information changes during a workflow—for example, replacing an estimate with an updated value.

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:33.836
Use reassignment carefully.

00:00:33.836 --> 00:00:40.062
The value may change, but the variable name should still describe the same kind of information.
